  "note": "Triennial urban council election of May 1949. No newspaper report has been found; the Belfast and Ulster Directory 1950 lists the twelve members of the council. Twelve members printed (chairman R. M'Afee; vice-chairman W. M'K. Dunlop), matching the twelve seats. Eleven were elected in 1946; A. Stuart, B.L. is new (J. Fullerton of 1946 is absent). Directory list, not an election report: the directory prints the council's membership as it stood when the edition was compiled (late in the year after the election). It does not say whether members were returned at a poll or unopposed, and cannot show co-options made between the election and compilation. No votes."
